      "kind": "grammar",
      "promptEs": "preposición + el que / la que / los que / las que",
      "questionEn": "How do you say “the one who” or “the ones who” after a short linking word such as a or con?",
      "answerEn": "Use el que, la que, los que, or las que to match the person or thing you mean.",
      "noteEn": "Que introduces the description, while the article identifies the unnamed person or thing. When a comes before el que, a + el contracts to al, producing al que.",
      "example": {
        "es": "Hablo con la que llegó primero.",
        "en": "I am speaking with the one who arrived first."
      },
      "tags": ["B1", "grammar", "relative expression", "contraction"]
